[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3314950859","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110722#issuecomment-3314950859","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110722","id":3314950859,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FliLL","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-20T12:48:23Z","updated_at":"2025-09-20T12:48:23Z","body":"Mmmm. I'm not sure how to feel about this, personally. To have the property exist, exposed, with setters and getters, but actually refer to an underlying metadata entry? All to save on memory. It sounds very hacky to me. One could argue `editor_description` shouldn't even be available in release builds, and yet it is.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3314950859/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3315047411","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110722#issuecomment-3315047411","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110722","id":3315047411,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Fl5vz","user":{"login":"MatthiasBae","id":52577744,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNTc3NzQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52577744?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthiasBae","html_url":"https://github.com/MatthiasBae","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthiasBae/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthiasBae/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthiasBae/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthiasBae/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthiasBae/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthiasBae/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthiasBae/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthiasBae/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthiasBae/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-20T15:20:13Z","updated_at":"2025-09-20T15:20:13Z","body":"> All to save on memory. It sounds very hacky to me. One could argue `editor_description` shouldn't even be available in release builds, and yet it is.\n\nI agree. I guess the additional memory is ignorable especially when using resources as only one reference exists. About how much memory are we talking about? Some bytes? Maybe Kb?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3315047411/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3315056486","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110722#issuecomment-3315056486","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110722","id":3315056486,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Fl79m","user":{"login":"chocola-mint","id":56677134,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2Njc3MTM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56677134?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint","html_url":"https://github.com/chocola-mint","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-20T15:32:49Z","updated_at":"2025-09-20T15:32:49Z","body":"> One could argue editor_description shouldn't even be available in release builds, and yet it is.\r\n\r\nAs the author of the other PR, I'd like to chime in here and say that theoretically if the resource exporter can detect editor-only properties (could be via PropertyHint, or could just be all properties that start with the prefix `editor_`) and just not serialize them, you can save memory that would otherwise be used on the editor-only properties.\r\n\r\nThis means that the properties technically still exist in the exported build, but as their entries in `.res` or `.tscn` don't exist there, they will just be initialized to their default values all the time. This has the added benefit of GDScript code that references editor-only properties (even indirectly guarded by `Engine.is_editor_hint()`) doesn't suddenly end up with compile errors in the build.\r\n\r\nIn this case, implementing editor description would not require using metadata and IMO would be a lot cleaner.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3315056486/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3315062627","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110722#issuecomment-3315062627","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110722","id":3315062627,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Fl9dj","user":{"login":"timothyqiu","id":372476,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MjQ3Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/372476?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu","html_url":"https://github.com/timothyqiu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-20T15:43:42Z","updated_at":"2025-09-20T15:43:42Z","body":"> To have the property exist, exposed, with setters and getters, but actually refer to an underlying metadata entry? All to save on memory.\r\n\r\nIt has to be an exposed property because it needs to be edited in the Inspector as \"Editor Description\". In other words, this is a compatibility measure.\r\n\r\nIf compatibility is not a concern, it doesn't have to be a property at all. It can be edited and viewed using a separate UI.\r\n\r\n> One could argue `editor_description` shouldn't even be available in release builds, and yet it is.\r\n\r\nOverall runtime footprint and the runtime footprint in exported projects are different concerns.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3315062627/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]